Full Binary Tree
Every node has either:

0 children
OR
2 children
Example:

        A
       / \
      B   C
     / \
    D   E
A → 2 children

B → 2 children

C → 0

D → 0

E → 0

Therefore, Full Binary Tree.

Complete Binary Tree
This is about position/filling, not number of children.

        A
       / \
      B   C
     / \ /
    D  E F
All levels are full except possibly the last, and the last level is filled left → right.

