❌ Q13 — Important Trap
Question:

Which statement is FALSE?

Correct:

C. Every binary tree is a BST.

This is false.

Binary tree
Only requirement:

Maximum 2 children
Example:

       10
      /  \
     50   2
This is a valid binary tree.

But it is not a BST, because:

50 > 10
yet 50 is on the left.

BST
Must satisfy:

LEFT < ROOT < RIGHT
So:

Every BST is a binary tree, but every binary tree is NOT a BST.

🔥 This is an exam-favorite statement.

